{"author":{"id":"a6ed2cdff32a5893420db55a64ed789141affa8969bcc91fe866ac2a8ed4c805"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1770345908,"nonce":"uvn1lW/9Rn4JqCJcYgSbixonZsA=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh87l7pl0","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1512#issuecomment-3857619316"},"message":"\u003e ... since capital letters are indeed valid hexadecimal, right \n\nThe are indeed, but the caching isn't normalizing the keys (i.e. `strings.ToLower`, so you won't find the entity you're looking for if you're not careful to always use the same case.\n\n```\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/git-bug/git-bug/commands/execenv\"\n\t\"github.com/git-bug/git-bug/entity\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n\targs := []string{\"611d1c0\"}\n\n\tenv := execenv.NewEnv()\n\tfn := execenv.LoadBackend(env)\n\tif err := fn(nil, args); err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(err)\n\t}\n\n\tb, _, err := env.Backend.Bugs().New(\"test(entity): verify entity IDs are lowercase\", \"Try to retrieve this bug with uppercase ID\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(err)\n\t}\n\n\t_, err = env.Backend.Bugs().Resolve(b.Id())\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(err)\n\t}\n\n\t// This errors with \"bug doesn't exist\"\n\t_, err = env.Backend.Bugs().ResolvePrefix(strings.ToUpper(b.Id().String()))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"ResolvePrefix:\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// This errors due to entity.Id.Validate with \"invalid id: invalid character\"\n\t_, err = env.Backend.Bugs().Resolve(entity.Id(strings.ToUpper(b.Id().String())))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"Resolve:\", err)\n\t}\n}\n```","files":null}]}